## Deploying your first application

All new Software Engineers are encouraged to deploy their first application early in onboarding.

The Golden Path tutorials guide you through deploying your first Java, Node.js or Python application and making your first change to it:

- [Golden path - Java](https://backstage.platform.hmcts.net/docs/default/component/golden-path-java)
- [Golden path - Node.js](https://backstage.platform.hmcts.net/docs/default/component/golden-path-nodejs)
- [Golden path - Python](https://backstage.hmcts.net/create/templates/default/fastapi-template)

## Docker Business Licence

To use Docker Desktop at HMCTS, you need a Docker Business licence linked to your Docker Hub account.

Docker Desktop version 4.4.0 and above redirects you to a web browser to sign in with SSO using your HMCTS email address.

To use the Docker CLI with your account, create a Personal Authentication Token (PAT).

See the [Docker access token documentation](https://docs.docker.com/docker-hub/access-tokens/).

You must be in one of the following groups:

- `DTS Platform Operations`
- `DTS CFT Developers`
- `DTS SDS Developers`
- `DTS Docker Hub`

